{"id":570,"slug":"the-silence","title":"The Silence","year":1963,"country":"Sweden","duration":95,"spine":211,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/570-the-silence","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/96e1add69295c206401f94f0ad905e63/3N8dRvaGxaUqSIYisqeX0KJpdn69Vw_large.jpg","description":"Two sisters—the sickly, intellectual Ester (Ingrid Thulin) and the sensual, pragmatic Anna (Gunnel Lindblom)—travel by train with Anna’s young son, Johan (Jörgen Lindström), to a foreign country that appears to be on the brink of war. Attempting to cope with their alien surroundings, each sister is left to her own vices while they vie for Johan’s affection, and in so doing sabotage what little remains of their relationship. Regarded as one of the most sexually provocative films of its day, Ingmar Bergman’s The Silence offers a disturbing vision of emotional isolation in a suffocating spiritual void.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Ingmar Bergman","slug":"ingmar-bergman"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Ingrid Thulin","role":"Ester","slug":"ingrid-thulin"},{"actor":"Gunnel Lindblom","role":"Anna","slug":"gunnel-lindblom"},{"actor":"Jörgen Lindström","role":"Johan","slug":"jorgen-lindstrom"},{"actor":"Birger Malmsten","role":"Bartender","slug":"birger-malmsten"},{"actor":"Håkan Jahnberg","role":"Hotel waiter","slug":"hakan-jahnberg"},{"actor":"Eduardo Gutiérrez and The Eduardinis","role":"The little people","slug":"eduardo-gutierrez-and-the-eduardinis"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Ingmar Bergman","slug":"ingmar-bergman"},{"role":"Written by","person":"Ingmar Bergman","slug":"ingmar-bergman"},{"role":"Cinematographer","person":"Sven Nykvist","slug":"sven-nykvist"},{"role":"Editor","person":"Ulla Ryghe","slug":null},{"role":"Assistant director","person":"Lenn Hjortzberg","slug":null},{"role":"Assistant director","person":"Lars-Erik Liedholm","slug":null},{"role":"Art director","person":"P. A. Lundgren","slug":null},{"role":"Production manager","